description: Route engineering work to the correct architecture document
alwaysApply: true
---

Before writing or modifying code, identify whether the task is backend, frontend, mobile, or
product, then consult the matching source of truth.

# Documentation authority

- `docs/SRS.md` — product and business requirements
- `ARCHITECTURE.md` — NestJS backend architecture
- `docs/FRONTEND-ARCHITECTURE.md` — React dashboard architecture (conventions only)
- `docs/MOBILE-ARCHITECTURE.md` — Expo React Native mobile architecture (conventions only)
- `docs/admin-dashboard-tasks.md` — admin / author / mobile STEP plan and delivery status
- `mobile/README.md` — mobile package runbook (commands, env, Replit); not architecture
- `docs/FUTURE.md` — deferred product work
- `docs/srs-coverage-matrix.md` — coverage tracking

Do not mix backend layering into frontend or mobile work. Do not mix React dashboard rules into
backend or mobile work. Do not modify `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/FRONTEND-ARCHITECTURE.md`,
`docs/MOBILE-ARCHITECTURE.md`, or `docs/SRS.md` unless the user explicitly requests it. Do not
update architecture documents to record STEP progress, install status, or remaining bootstrap.
Use `docs/admin-dashboard-tasks.md`.

# How to choose

- Changes under `backend/` or `ARCHITECTURE.md` → follow `ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Changes under `frontend/` or `docs/FRONTEND-ARCHITECTURE.md` → follow `docs/FRONTEND-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Changes under `mobile/` or `docs/MOBILE-ARCHITECTURE.md` → follow `docs/MOBILE-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Shared repo files (`pnpm-workspace.yaml`, root `package.json`, Cursor rules) → keep architecture
  documents consistent; do not invent a fourth architecture

If a user request conflicts with the governing architecture document:

1. Identify the conflict clearly.
2. Explain the architectural consequence.
3. Ask for or follow an explicit user override when necessary.
